## Why

{% if uat %}Production's data lives in `{{ slug }}`. Every other deployment reads `uat-{{ slug }}`, so
production's data never reaches a preview.{% else %}The build's database lives in `{{ slug }}`.
Each preview gets a branch of it.{% endif %}

## Steps

1. In the Neon console, open the client's organisation.
2. Make the project `{{ slug }}` for production, in the region nearest to the Vercel functions.
{%- if uat %}
3. Make the project `uat-{{ slug }}` for UAT, in the same region.
4. Put test data only in `uat-{{ slug }}`. Never copy production's rows into it.
{%- endif %}
{% if uat %}5{% else %}3{% endif %}. Compare the project names with the column `Database` of `.icm/environments.md`.
   If a name is different, correct the column.

## Done when

- [ ] The project `{{ slug }}` exists.
{%- if uat %}
- [ ] The project `uat-{{ slug }}` exists, with test data only.
{%- endif %}
- [ ] The column `Database` of `.icm/environments.md` names `{{ slug }}`{% if uat %} and `uat-{{ slug }}`{% endif %}.
